# VitePress Theme Guidelines

Keep customizations minimal. The default VitePress theme is already excellent — we override only what's necessary for our personality.

## CSS Architecture

- All custom CSS lives exclusively in `.vitepress/theme/custom.css`
- Theme entry point: `.vitepress/theme/index.ts` — extends default theme only
- Zero inline styles in markdown files
- Zero new Vue components unless absolutely necessary

## CSS Variables

Use CSS variables for everything. Never hardcode hex values directly in rules.

Define overrides in `:root` and `html.dark` (VitePress uses `class="dark"` on `<html>`, not `data-theme`):

```css
/* Light mode */
:root {
  --vp-c-brand-1: #646cff;   /* primary accent */
  --vp-c-brand-2: #535bf2;
  --vp-c-brand-3: #344e83;
  --vp-c-brand-soft: rgba(100, 108, 255, 0.14);
}

/* Dark mode */
html.dark {
  --vp-c-brand-1: #7c8aff;
  --vp-c-brand-2: #6b74ff;
  --vp-c-brand-3: #4d5fd1;
  --vp-c-brand-soft: rgba(124, 138, 255, 0.14);
}
```

## Color Palette

We use a distinctive violet-indigo accent (not the default blue/purple of most docs sites):
- Primary: violet-indigo gradient feel (`#7c8aff` to `#535bf2`)
- Danger: coral-red (`#f43f5e`)
- Tip: teal (`#14b8a6`)
- Warning: amber (`#f59e0b`)

## Typography

Override for readability:

```css
:root {
  --vp-font-family-base: '"Noto Sans SC", "PingFang SC", "Microsoft YaHei", sans-serif';
  --vp-font-family-mono: '"JetBrains Mono", "Fira Code", "Cascadia Code", monospace';
  --vp-doc-line-height: 1.8;  /* looser than default */
}
```

## Code Block Styling

Custom code block header to show file names:

```css
.vp-code-group .tabs {
  font-size: 0.85rem;
  font-family: var(--vp-font-family-mono);
}
```

## Sidebar

Keep VitePress default sidebar. Only override:
- Collapsed group indicator style
- Active link highlight color

## Dark Mode

All custom styles MUST have dark mode equivalents. Test by toggling the theme.

```css
/* Light only */
:root { /* ... */ }

/* Dark only */
html.dark { /* ... */ }
```

Never use `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)` — VitePress handles theme switching via `html.dark`.

## Favicon & Logo

- Place in `docs/public/`
- Reference in `.vitepress/config.js` via `src` assets
- Current: use a simple SVG icon (inline in config) as placeholder
